  <h3>Galley extractor <span class="tag">extractor · part: fan belt</span></h3>
  <p class="note">No extractor machine is in the game today (Deck 3's stand-in dropped out when the galley plant was built; <code>2-extractor-1</code> on Deck 2 is a scrubber). The table is kept for when one is added; the galley alarm incident uses the galley plant.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th><th>Card</th><th>Up close</th><th>When</th><th>How common</th><th>Still</th><th>From</th></tr>
    <tr><td>The fan belt is slipping</td><td>fan belt</td><td>weak draw</td><td>a squeal at start, smoke lingers</td><td>after use</td><td>●●●</td><td>"New belt. Still weak: the hood's filter's black."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The hood filter is clogged</td><td>filter</td><td>weak draw</td><td>grease dripping at the hood's edge</td><td>always</td><td>●●</td><td>"Clean filter. Still weak, and it squeals."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The motor relay is sticking</td><td>relay</td><td>stops and starts</td><td>clicks, runs, stops</td><td>warm</td><td>●</td><td>"New belt. Still stops and starts."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
  </table></div>

  <h3>Cold store chiller <span class="tag">chiller · Deck 3 · part: compressor</span></h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th><th>Card</th><th>Up close</th><th>When</th><th>How common</th><th>Still</th><th>From</th></tr>
    <tr><td>The compressor is labouring</td><td>compressor</td><td>runs warm</td><td>a laboured hum that never stops</td><td>always</td><td>●●</td><td>"New compressor. Still warm: frost round the door."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The door seal is worn</td><td>seal</td><td>runs warm</td><td>frost round the door frame</td><td>after use (deliveries)</td><td>●●●</td><td>"Fresh seal. Still warm, and it hums all night."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The fan bearing is going</td><td>bearing</td><td>runs warm</td><td>warm at the back shelves, a rattle</td><td>always</td><td>●</td><td>"New bearing. Still warm by the door."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The temperature sensor reads wrong</td><td>signal card</td><td>milk going off (display fine)</td><td>the display says 3°, the back shelf feels warmer</td><td>always</td><td>●</td><td>"New compressor. Display still says 3°; still warm."</td><td>Senior Officer (P4)</td></tr>
  </table></div>

  <h3>Washer <span class="tag">washer · Deck 4 laundry · part: pump</span></h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th><th>Card</th><th>Up close</th><th>When</th><th>How common</th><th>Still</th><th>From</th></tr>
    <tr><td>The pump is failing</td><td>pump</td><td>leaks</td><td>a puddle under it, the pump housing damp</td><td>after use</td><td>●●●</td><td>"New pump. Still drips at the door."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The door seal is worn</td><td>seal</td><td>leaks</td><td>drips at the door during the spin</td><td>after use</td><td>●●</td><td>"Fresh seal. Still a puddle under it."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The drain valve is sticking</td><td>valve</td><td>leaks</td><td>water left in the drum after the cycle</td><td>after use</td><td>●●</td><td>"New valve. Still a puddle under it."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The drum bearing is going</td><td>bearing</td><td>loud spin</td><td>a rumble, the machine walks on the floor</td><td>after use</td><td>●</td><td>"New pump. Still rumbles."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>The control relay is sticking</td><td>relay</td><td>stops mid-cycle</td><td>stops, clicks, starts again</td><td>warm</td><td>●</td><td>"New pump. Still stops mid-cycle."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">The washer is Day 5's first head-scratcher (P3): pump, door seal and drain valve all show "leaks".</p>

  <h3>Main lift <span class="tag">lift · the spine · part: relay</span></h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th><th>Card</th><th>Up close</th><th>When</th><th>How common</th><th>Still</th><th>From</th></tr>
    <tr><td>The control relay is sticking</td><td>relay</td><td>slow, stops at decks</td><td>pauses before the doors open</td><td>warm (busy hours)</td><td>●●●</td><td>"New bearing. Still pauses at the doors."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>A guide bearing is worn</td><td>bearing</td><td>judders</td><td>a grinding in the shaft between decks</td><td>always</td><td>●●</td><td>"New relay. Still judders between decks."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Its breaker trips</td><td>breaker</td><td>stops between decks</td><td>stalls, then the breaker light</td><td>at peak (shift change)</td><td>●</td><td>"New relay. It still stalls at shift change."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">A judder only at one deck is the lift-roof head-scratcher later (M17, side job).</p>

  <h3>Light relays <span class="tag">lights · Decks 1 and 3 (real); part: relay</span></h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th><th>Card</th><th>Up close</th><th>When</th><th>How common</th><th>Still</th><th>From</th></tr>
    <tr><td>A relay sticks when warm</td><td>relay</td><td>lights flicker</td><td>the whole room's lights, worse after an hour</td><td>warm</td><td>●●●</td><td>"New lamp. Still flickers, the whole room."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>A lamp is at its end</td><td>lamp</td><td>lights flicker</td><td>one lamp only</td><td>always</td><td>●●</td><td>"New relay. That one lamp still flickers."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>A breaker trips</td><td>breaker</td><td>lights out</td><td>a whole run dark; the breaker's lamp lit</td><td>at peak</td><td>●</td><td>"New relay. Dark again at dinner."</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Wiring loose behind the panel</td><td>cable</td><td>lights flicker</td><td>flickers when the door slams</td><td>touched</td><td>●</td><td>"New relay. Still flickers when the door goes."</td><td>Officer</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Its setting has drifted</td><td>tune</td><td>lights flicker / lights dim</td><td>fast flicker everywhere (high) or a sag (low)</td><td>always</td><td>●●</td><td>—</td><td>Day 4</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">"Reset the breaker: fine for an hour, then back" is the warm relay's clue for later, harder P3 cases (it rules out the lamp, the breaker and the wiring at once, so it's never the only clue).</p>

