<section id="t2">
  <h2>Tier 2 machines (draft, finished with Step 3)</h2>
  <p class="note">Three causes each for now (part, sign); Step 3 adds the up-close signs, the "still" lines and the load and traced causes (M9: a symptom on one machine, the cause on another).</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Kind</th><th>Card</th><th>Causes (fix: what you see)</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Air scrubber (<code>scrubber</code>)</td><td>stuffy air</td><td>filter clogged (filter: a grey grille); fan bearing (bearing: a whine); fan and flow drifted (tune, stage 2: hum off pitch)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Heating plant (<code>heater</code>)</td><td>cold cabins</td><td>valve sticking (valve: one branch cold); circulation pump (pump: all cool, a knock); control relay (relay: on and off)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Water recycler (<code>recycler</code>)</td><td>weak showers</td><td>membrane fouled (membrane: weak all day); pump can't keep up (pump: weak only after 18:00); valve sticking (valve: one deck weak)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Water filter bank (<code>filter</code>)</td><td>cloudy water</td><td>a cartridge spent (cartridge: one housing slow); a seal leaking (seal: damp floor); the bypass valve open (valve: clear then cloudy)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Heating pumps (<code>heatpump</code>)</td><td>cold cabins</td><td>pump (pump: a knock); bearing (bearing: a whine); valve (valve: one side cold)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pipe valves (<code>valve</code>)</td><td>low pressure</td><td>valve sticking (valve); a seal weeping (seal: a drip)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Oxygen cells (<code>o2cell</code>)</td><td>air thin</td><td>a cell spent (oxygen cell); the regulator (regulator: a hiss)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Electrolyser (<code>electrolyser</code>)</td><td>air thin</td><td>membrane (membrane); a cell (cell); the relay (relay: stops and starts)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Circulation pumps (<code>pump</code>)</td><td>low flow</td><td>pump (pump); bearing (bearing: grinding); seal (seal: a drip)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>UV steriliser (<code>uv</code>)</td><td>water tastes off</td><td>UV lamp spent (uv lamp: a dull glow); relay (relay); seal (seal)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Irrigation pumps (<code>irrigation</code>)</td><td>dry beds</td><td>pump (pump); a valve (valve: one bed dry); nozzles clogged (filter: spits, then nothing; M14)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Nutrient dosing (<code>nutrient</code>)</td><td>yellow leaves</td><td>nutrient pack (nutrient pack); pump (pump); regulator (regulator: doses too much)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Air plant (<code>airplant</code>)</td><td>stuffy air ship-wide</td><td>filter (filter); bearing (bearing); fan belt (fan belt: a squeal)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Main fan (<code>fan</code>)</td><td>stuffy air ship-wide</td><td>bearing (bearing: a rumble); fan belt (fan belt); relay (relay: stops)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Manifold (<code>manifold</code>)</td><td>one deck cold or weak</td><td>a valve (valve: that deck's branch); a seal (seal); the regulator (regulator)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lab gas plant (<code>gasplant</code>)</td><td>low lab gas</td><td>regulator (regulator); seal (seal: a hiss); valve (valve)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Bay door gear (<code>doorgear</code>)</td><td>bay doors slow</td><td>seal (seal: a draught); bearing (bearing: a judder); relay (relay: stops halfway)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat S: section 17's <code>FAULT_CAUSES</code>)</h2>
  <div class="lines">FAULT_CAUSES.washer = [
  { id: 'pump',  part: 'pump',  w: 3, shows: 'leaks', sign: 'puddle under it', when: 'after-use', still: 'washer.pump' },
  { id: 'seal',  part: 'seal',  w: 2, shows: 'leaks', sign: 'drips at the door', when: 'after-use', still: 'washer.seal' },
  { id: 'valve', part: 'valve', w: 2, shows: 'leaks', sign: 'water left in the drum', when: 'after-use', still: 'washer.valve' },
  { id: 'bearing', part: 'bearing', w: 1, shows: 'loud spin', ... },
  { id: 'relay', part: 'relay', w: 1, shows: 'stops mid-cycle', when: 'warm', ... } ]
// a setting:  { id: 'drift', setting: true, w: 2, shows: 'runs hot|runs cool', from: 4 }        (M5)
// a load:     { id: 'junction', load: '3-junction-…', w: 1, shows: 'runs cool', when: 'peak', band: 'T2' }  (P1)
// band:       'T2' / 'T3' = only as a suspect (and only as a real cause) in that band or later</div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Texts</b> (<code>shows</code>, <code>sign</code>, <code>still</code>) are keys into the Works writer's <code>content/works/faults.lines</code>; the plain words above are the first draft of those lines.</li>
    <li><b>The pick</b> (foundation 17.4): only causes allowed at the machine's band and day (<code>from</code>: a setting from Day 4; <code>band</code>), weighted by <code>w</code> × (1 + the part's wear share); a <code>load</code> is never picked as a real fault's cause on its own (it only appears in head-scratchers that say so).</li>
    <li><b>Same card, different signs:</b> within a kind, causes sharing a <code>shows</code> must have different <code>sign</code>s (the scanner relies on it: when two parts read low, the sign tells them apart).</li>
    <li><b>Parts:</b> every part here is in <code>STOCK</code> today; <code>compressor</code> has only 2 (fine: rare) and <code>signal card</code> 2.</li>
    <li><b>Corrections to the plan:</b> the plan's Tier 1 list named the power junction and the bay door gear; in the game they're Tier 3 (<code>junction</code>) and Tier 2 (<code>doorgear</code>), so the junction appears only as a <i>load</i> suspect (P1) and the door gear is in the Tier 2 list. The Tier 1 kinds are the game's: oven, range, galley plant, extractor, chiller, washer, lift, light relays, cart dock, grow lights.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="check" class="builder">
  <h2>Checks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b><code>machine_check</code></b>: every Tier 1 kind has a table; every part is in <code>STOCK</code>; no two causes of a kind share both <code>shows</code> and <code>sign</code>; the picked cause the same twice; over 14 days every Tier 1 kind's causes all appear and the common ones most.</li>
    <li><b><code>puzzle_check</code></b>: P3 fits the washer (three "leaks"), the lights (three "flicker"), the oven (three "runs cool") and the extractor (two "weak draw" + the relay: no, so P3 skips it on T1: fine).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Builders' questions</h2>
  <p class="note">Questions from builders and the answers go here (ask the Pillar 5 designer through the lead). None yet.</p>
</section>
